Phone Booth is a 2002 American psychological thriller film directed by Joel Schumacher, produced by David Zucker and Gil Netter,
written by Larry Cohen and starring Colin Farrell, Forest Whitaker, Katie Holmes, Radha Mitchell, and Kiefer Sutherland.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
In the film, a malevolent hidden sniper calls a phone booth, and when a young
publicist inside answers the phone, he quickly finds his life is at risk.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Produced by Fox 2000 Pictures and Zucker/Netter Productions, the film premiered at the 2002 Toronto
International Film Festival, and was set to be theatrically released in November 2002, but the D.C.

